# Agent Quality Gates

Apply these gates before any commit or push.
Use `docs/agent-templates.md` as the canonical format for release-note snippets and post-merge verification checklists.

## Test Agent Requirements
- Run checks relevant to changed scope:
  - Lint for touched files/modules
  - Targeted tests for changed behavior
  - Build/type-check when change impact is broad
- Prefer targeted test selection over full-suite runs when appropriate.
- Report:
  - Commands executed
  - Pass/fail status
  - Failing test names and likely root cause (if any)

## Commit Readiness Policy
- Commits are allowed only after required checks pass.
- If checks fail:
  - Prefer fix-first and re-run checks
  - Do not commit unless user explicitly approves bypassing
- Include test evidence in delivery summary for each commit.

## Git Safety
- Never commit secrets (`.env`, credentials, private keys, tokens).
- Exclude unrelated personal/non-code files unless user explicitly requests inclusion.
- Use clear commit messages describing intent and user-visible impact.

## Documentation Gate
- If behavior, setup, or operations changed, update `README.md` and/or relevant docs in same delivery cycle.

## Release Notes Snippet (mandatory)
- Delivery agent must produce a short user-facing changelog entry for every commit/push.
- Use the "Release Notes Snippet" template in `docs/agent-templates.md`.

## Post-Merge Verification (mandatory)
- After push/merge, confirm and report:
  - Use the "Post-Merge Verification" template in `docs/agent-templates.md`.
